  "question": "This database is intended to record information related to political parties, candidates, voters, and voting activities. The system will support the following operations:\nPolitical Parties: Record the basic information about political parties, including name and description. The system should support the ability to add, delete, and modify political party information.\nCandidates: Record basic information about candidates, including their name, the political party they belong to, and whether they have industry connections. The system should allow adding, deleting, and modifying candidate information.\nVoters: Record basic information about voters, including their name, email, and the creation time of their registration. The system should support adding, deleting, and modifying voter information.\nVoting Records: Record each voting activity, including the voter ID, candidate ID, and the time of voting. The system ensures that each voter can only vote once.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0082\n\nCREATE TABLE `political_party` (\n  `party_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`party_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `candidate` (\n  `candidate_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `party_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `has_industry_connections` tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`candidate_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `candidate_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`party_id`) REFERENCES `political_party` (`party_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `voter` (\n  `voter_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`voter_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `email` (`email`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `voting_record` (\n  `voting_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `voter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `candidate_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `voted_at` datetime NOT NULL DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`voting_record_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `voter_id` (`voter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `voting_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`voter_id`) REFERENCES `voter` (`voter_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `voting_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`candidate_id`) REFERENCES `candidate` (`candidate_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
